{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XMPHNqhrYYmvwge8kbAYMT","type":"tool_result","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Regression gate for loop0013 (the duality gap of the lower-bound obstruction families, by search).\n\nPasses only if all five hold:\n1. `lake build` in lean/ succeeds;\n2. every `.lean` file under lean/MOSPFormalization/ (top level, Complex/ and\n   Search/) is imported by lean/MOSPFormalization.lean, so the build really\n   checks it;\n3. the number of `sorry` in Lean *code* (comments and docstrings stripped) is\n   at most the baseline (0: the development has none since Appendix E) plus\n   the entries in allowed_sorries.txt, and no `axiom` declaration exists;\n4. `python -m pytest tests/ -q -x` passes, and so does `pytest` in\n   pathwidth_solver/;\n5. the paper builds with no undefined references (`make -C paper1/latex check`).\n\n    python3 Ralph_Loops/loop0013/gate.py\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport re\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nREPO = HERE.parents[1]\nLEAN = REPO / \"lean\"\nBASELINE_SORRIES = 0\nALLOWED = HERE / \"allowed_sorries.txt\"\nPAPER = REPO / \"paper1\" / \"latex\"\n\n\ndef strip_comments(src: str) -> str:\n    out, i, depth = [], 0, 0\n    while i < len(src):\n        if src.startswith(\"/-\", i):\n            depth += 1; i += 2; continue\n        if depth and src.startswith(\"-/\", i):\n            depth -= 1; i += 2; continue\n        if depth:\n            i += 1; continue\n        if src.startswith(\"--\", i):\n            j = src.find(\"\\n\", i); i = len(src) if j < 0 else j; continue\n        if src[i] == '\"':\n            j = i + 1\n            while j < len(src) and src[j] != '\"':\n                j += 2 if src[j] == \"\\\\\" else 1\n            i = j + 1; continue\n        out.append(src[i]); i += 1\n    return \"\".join(out)\n\n\ndef _main() -> int:\n    ok = True\n    b = subprocess.run([\"lake\", \"build\"], cwd=LEAN, capture_output=True, text=True, errors=\"replace\")\n    tail = \"\\n\".join((b.stdout + b.stderr).splitlines()[-25:])\n    if b.returncode != 0:\n        print(\"GATE FAIL: lake build\\n\" + tail); return 1\n    print(\"lake build: ok\")\n\n    root = (LEAN / \"MOSPFormalization.lean\").read_text()\n    for f in sorted((LEAN / \"MOSPFormalization\").rglob(\"*.lean\")):\n        mod = \"MOSPFormalization.\" + \".\".join(f.relative_to(LEAN / \"MOSPFormalization\").with_suffix(\"\").parts)\n        if not re.search(rf\"^import {re.escape(mod)}\\s*$\", root, re.M):\n            print(f\"GATE FAIL: {mod} is not imported by MOSPFormalization.lean\"); ok = False\n\n    sorries, axioms = [], []\n    for f in sorted((LEAN / \"MOSPFormalization\").rglob(\"*.lean\")):\n        code = strip_comments(f.read_text())\n        for n, line in enumerate(code.splitlines(), 1):\n            if re.search(r\"\\bsorry\\b\", line):\n                sorries.append(f\"{f.relative_to(LEAN)}:{n}\")\n            if re.match(r\"\\s*(private\\s+)?axiom\\b\", line):\n                axioms.append(f\"{f.relative_to(LEAN)}:{n}\")\n    allowed = [l for l in ALLOWED.read_text().splitlines() if l.strip() and not l.startswith(\"#\")] if ALLOWED.exists() else []\n    limit = BASELINE_SORRIES + len(allowed)\n    print(f\"sorry in code: {len(sorries)} (limit {limit}): {sorries}\")\n    if len(sorries) > limit:\n        print(\"GATE FAIL: more sorry than the baseline plus allowed_sorries.txt\"); ok = False\n    if axioms:\n        print(f\"GATE FAIL: axiom declarations: {axioms}\"); ok = False\n\n    t = subprocess.run([sys.executable, \"-m\", \"pytest\", \"tests/\", \"-q\", \"-x\"], cwd=REPO, timeout=2400,\n                       capture_output=True, text=True, errors=\"replace\")\n    print(\"\\n\".join((t.stdout + t.stderr).splitlines()[-5:]))\n    if t.returncode != 0:\n        print(\"GATE FAIL: pytest\"); ok = False\n    w = subprocess.run([sys.executable, \"-m\", \"pytest\", \"-q\", \"-p\", \"no:cacheprovider\"], timeout=2400,\n                       cwd=REPO / \"pathwidth_solver\", capture_output=True, text=True, errors=\"replace\")\n    print(\"\\n\".join((w.stdout + w.stderr).splitlines()[-3:]))\n    if w.returncode != 0:\n        print(\"GATE FAIL: pathwidth_solver pytest\"); ok = False\n    # The paper must build cleanly: no undefined references or citations.\n    m = subprocess.run([\"make\", \"check\"], cwd=PAPER, capture_output=True, text=True, errors=\"replace\")\n    print(\"\\n\".join((m.stdout + m.stderr).splitlines()[-3:]))\n    if m.returncode != 0:\n        print(\"GATE FAIL: paper1/latex make check\"); ok = False\n    print(\"GATE PASS\" if ok else \"GATE FAIL\")\n    return 0 if ok else 1\n\n\n\n\ndef main() -> int:  # added 2026-11-02: a hung pytest (libgomp fork deadlock) held loop0012's gate for 13 h\n    try:\n        return _main()\n    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired as e:\n        print(f\"GATE FAIL: timeout in {e.cmd}\")\n        return 1\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n----\n  loop0010's `large@recorded` run left five more), 7 of them tight; the\n  survey's file-less 54 (`4-1_0`) and 92 (`8-2_0`) are carried as\n  `minor_survey`, outside `floor0`. Chu & Stuckey by class: mean `floor0` gap\n  0.2 / 0.2 / 0.64 / 2.72 / 6.64 / 4.96 at 30–125 customers; Harper carries\n  the dense classes (`125-125-10` gap 0.2), minors the ridge (`125-125-2`\n  4 of 5 closed), and nothing on record reaches the sparse 100s\n  (`100-100-2` gap 7.8). `optimum > tw_hi + 1` on 564 instances, 156 of the\n  338. Dataset: cheap floors tight on 5,231 of 16,636 (31.4%); MMD+\n  least-c the best (5,059 tight); 0 of 430 `certified:minor` classes tight\n  (gap 4.6); 22 VSPLIB grids with a component above 1,024 vertices skipped\n  for those components; 17 clique enumerations censored; no \"header-only\"\n  rows exist in the jsonl (the brief's 78 is not reproduced); 5 of 430 minor\n  rows carry no certificate; all 425 certificates refute `width − 1`.\n- **Targets frozen** (`targets.json`, seed 0): `gap338` 338, `cs200` 200,\n  `open24` 24 (floors from `results_quick.csv` and\n  `results_quick_rescued.csv`, not `results.csv` as plan §0.3 says),\n  `rest500` 500 (stratified 345 / 140 / 11 / 3 / 0 / 1 / 0 over the bands:\n  the pool has nothing above 100 customers outside `gap338 ∪ cs200`),\n  `small` 4,123. The test re-derives `rest500` from the ledger and the seed.\n- **Kill verdict**: none for the item; guard passed. The harness's validity\n  stage (\"above optimum\" must be 0) was not re-run: the ledger's guard is\n  that check, applied to every bound column on every corpus instance.\n- **Gate: PASS** (`reports/scratch/obstruction_search/01_ledger/gate_run.out`):\n  lake build ok, 0 sorry, 0 axiom; `tests/` 1,816 passed, 2 skipped, 1 xfailed\n  (4:43); `pathwidth_solver/` 123 passed (8:01, under the owner's load of\n  27); paper 77 pages, no undefined references.\n\n### Blockers\n\nNone. One correction to the plan recorded in the report: the open classes'\nfloors live in `results_quick*.csv`, and the file-backed minor certificates\nnumber twelve, not seven.\n\n### Next\n\nItem 02 (family E by search: the ceiling on every target, exact `f` and `s*`\nat `n ≤ 22`, the floor by branch and bound). It reads `targets.json` and\n`ledger_corpus.csv` (`harper12`, its levels and caps are the family's floor on\nrecord; the 35 censored instances are where the SAT half of item 03 is\nneeded). Compute used by item 01: 1.01 core-hours of its 1.5.\n----\n M Ralph_Loops/loop0013/PROGRESS.md\n M Ralph_Loops/loop0013/iterations.md\n?? Ralph_Loops/loop0013/loop.log\n?? Ralph_Loops/loop0013/nohup.out\n?? Ralph_Loops/loop0013/session_it01.jsonl\n?? Ralph_Loops/loop0013/session_it01.log\n?? Ralph_Loops/loop0013/session_it01_fix1.jsonl\n?? Ralph_Loops/loop0013/session_it01_fix1.log\n?? Ralph_Loops/loop0013/status.json\n?? learning/obstruction_ledger.py\n?? reports/obstruction_search.md\n?? r